00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:35,000
and I was wondering what you thought was the spirit behind the requirements.

198
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:41,000
It seems some Scoutmasters give boys credit for merely attempting to do some of the cooking requirements, for example,

199
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:47,000
while other Scoutmasters require a high level of proficiency before they sign it.

200
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:53,000
The way I read it, it seems if a boy does the requirement, regardless of how well he's completed it,

201
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:58,000
how do you make sure that the same standard is applied across an entire troop

202
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:03,000
if everyone, from the Scoutmaster down to patrol leaders, are signing off on requirements?

203
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:06,000
David, you touched on a couple of important questions there.

204
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:11,000
So the difference between two basic approaches

205
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:16,000
You said, I believe if a boy does a requirement, regardless of how well he did it,

206
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,000
then he's completed the requirement.

207
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:23,000
and you've seen other Scoutmasters who really require a lot of practice and proficiency

208
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,000
before they sign the requirement.

209
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:29,000
That's really. I'll tell you. that's not an either or

